Note that you'll need to replace `keystore.jks` and `myAlias` with the actual path and name of your keystore file, as well as the alias of your signing certificate. Additionally, if you don't provide a password, an empty string (`""`) will be used.

The `Sign.sign()` method is not a standard Java method; it's assumed that you have implemented this method elsewhere in your code to perform the actual signing using the Java signing tool.

