function addUserData($name, $email, $verificationCode) {
    // Database connection
    $conn = mysqli_connect("localhost", "username", "password", "database");

    if (!$conn) {
        die("Connection failed: " . mysqli_connect_error());
    }

    // Query to insert data into the database
    $query = "INSERT INTO users (name, email) VALUES ('$name', '$email')";

    // Check verification code
    if ($verificationCode == "123456") { // Replace with your verification code
        if (mysqli_query($conn, $query)) {
            return "Data added successfully!";
        } else {
            return "Error adding data: " . mysqli_error($conn);
        }
    } else {
        return "Invalid verification code";
    }

    // Close connection
    mysqli_close($conn);
}
```

Remember to replace `"localhost"`, `"username"`, `"password"`, and `"database"` with your actual MySQL server details, and `"123456"` with your actual verification code. This function uses the `mysqli` extension for database operations, which is more secure than the old `mysql_*` functions.

